 - `autoMemoryEnabled` — enable Claude Code's auto-memory system (default `false`)
 - `pathToClaudeCodeExecutable` — path to the `claude` binary. Useful if your OS/filesystem has the SDK's bundled musl/glibc binaries in a place where they can't run. For example, with Nix you can set the binary to e.g. `"/home/you/.nix-profile/bin/claude"`.
 
+`cacheWarming` keeps an idle session's prompt cache alive, so returning to it after a break reads the conversation from the cache instead of re-writing all of it:
+- `enabled` — default `false`
+- `idleWindowMinutes` — how long after a session's last turn to keep it warm (default `120`)
+- `minPromptTokens` — skip sessions whose context is smaller than this (default `20000`)
+
+On subscription auth, Claude Code writes one-hour cache entries. A session that sits idle longer re-writes its whole context on the next turn, at twice the input price; a cache read costs a tenth to a twentieth of the input price, so the re-write is 20–40× a read. With warming on, when a session's run settles, the bridge resumes its Claude Code session 54 minutes after the last request, with that turn's options, forked and unpersisted, and stops the request at `message_start`. Prefill is done by then, so the cached prefix has been read and its hour restarted; no output is generated, and nothing is written to the session pi resumes. The first refresh also writes the short prompt tail; later ones read it back. Each refresh therefore costs one cache read of the context, and over a 12-hour window the 13 refreshes cost about a third of one re-write.
+
+Warming stops at the session's next query, at the end of the window, after compaction, tree navigation, `/new`, `/resume` or shutdown, and when a refresh comes back cold (a read of nothing, or a write over a tenth of the read). It applies only to sessions with a UI, not to headless subagent sessions, and only to one-hour entries: five-minute ones (API keys) would need a refresh every 4.5 minutes. Refreshes run in the pi process, so they stop when pi exits, and after a suspend that outlasts the entry. They count toward plan usage but not pi's session totals, which extensions can't add to. Claude Code hooks fire on them as on any turn (`UserPromptSubmit`, `SessionEnd`).
+
 
 **Notices:** the startup notice points out when `provider.plan` is unset and records `startupNoticeShown` in the global config. There's also a deprecation notice on first use of AskClaude that records its display date as `askClaudeDeprecationShown`.
 
